## 1. Scope

This audit covers CI, test coverage shape, deployment readiness docs, image/build workflows, security/supply-chain gates, SDK contract tests, production auth documentation, runtime governance tests, and whether the repo evidence supports benchmark-level production claims. It inspects both `ophanix-platform` and `ophanix-python-sdk`, including GitHub workflows, product tests, frontend scripts, deployment docs, package metadata, and SDK tests. Relevant benchmarks are Temporal production reliability, LangSmith/LangGraph deployment and eval readiness, JFrog supply-chain gates, Microsoft/AWS/Google enterprise readiness, and OpenAI/Arcade SDK ergonomics. Out of scope: individual feature implementation details, covered in the other feature reports.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Product Platform has substantial Python tests under `packages/product-platform/tests`, frontend scripts for unit/e2e/validation in `frontend/package.json`, deployment docs under `packages/product-platform/deploy/cloud`, image workflows in `.github/workflows/product-platform-images.yml`, general CI in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, dependency/supply-chain workflows, and SBOM workflow. Product docs honestly describe controlled internal/design partner SDK pilot readiness rather than full enterprise certification. The standalone SDK has tests using `httpx.MockTransport`, package metadata in `ophanix-python-sdk/pyproject.toml`, and publish workflow in `.github/workflows/publish.yml`.

Current workflow: many unit/integration tests validate product behavior, but CI coverage for product frontend, Postgres-backed product tests, images, live SDK contract, OIDC/JWKS, runtime crash recovery, plugin/MCP provenance, and deployment smoke is incomplete or uneven.

